## **SECTION 4: CORE FUNCTIONALITY & STATE MANAGEMENT**
*[Primary Assignment: Kimi - State Machine Logic | Secondary: CodeX - Audio Handling]*

### 4.1 Recording State Machine
```kotlin
sealed class RecordingState {
    object Idle : RecordingState()
    data class Recording(
        val mode: RecordingMode,
        val startTime: Long,
        val audioBuffer: CircularByteBuffer
    ) : RecordingState()
    object Processing : RecordingState()
    data class Error(val message: String) : RecordingState()
}

enum class RecordingMode {
    PUSH_TO_TALK,      // Hold to record, release to stop
    HANDS_FREE         // Tap to start, auto-stop on silence/volume
}
```

### 4.2 Input Handling Logic
**Touch Event Processing:**
```kotlin
// Pseudocode for Mic Button TouchListener
when (event.action) {
    ACTION_DOWN -> {
        startTime = System.currentTimeMillis()
        handler.postDelayed(handsFreeRunnable, 800) // 800ms threshold
        startVisualFeedback()
    }
    ACTION_UP -> {
        val duration = System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime
        handler.removeCallbacks(handsFreeRunnable)
        
        if (duration < 800) {
            // Tap detected - Enter Hands-Free mode
            if (currentState is Recording && currentState.mode == HANDS_FREE) {
                stopRecording() // Toggle off
            } else {
                startRecording(HANDS_FREE)
            }
        } else {
            // Hold-and-release - Push to talk stop
            stopRecording()
        }
    }
}
```

### 4.3 Audio Recording Specifications
**Configuration:**
- **Source:** `MediaRecorder.AudioSource.VOICE_RECOGNITION` (optimized for voice, noise suppression)
- **Sample Rate:** 16000 Hz (Groq optimal)
- **Channel:** Mono (CHANNEL_IN_MONO)
- **Encoding:** 16-bit PCM (ENCODING_PCM_16BIT)
- **Buffer Size:** `AudioRecord.getMinBufferSize() * 2` (prevent overflow)

**Hands-Free Mode Logic:**
- **Voice Activity Detection (VAD):** Simple amplitude threshold (500ms silence = stop)
- **Max Duration:** 5 minutes (prevent memory issues)
- **Pre-buffer:** Optional 300ms lookback to capture start of speech

### 4.4 Text Manipulation (InputConnection)
**Commit Strategy:**
- `InputConnection.setComposingText()` while processing (shows underline)
- `InputConnection.finishComposingText()` + `commitText()` when Groq returns
- **Backspace:** `InputConnection.deleteSurroundingText(1, 0)` with UTF-16 surrogate pair handling
- **Space:** `commitText(" ", 1)` with auto-capitalization detection (check `EditorInfo.inputType`)

**Editor Compatibility:**
- Handle `InputType.TYPE_TEXT_FLAG_NO_SUGGESTIONS` (don't show composing text)
- Respect `IME_FLAG_NO_ENTER_ACTION` (don't submit forms)
- Support `InputType.TYPE_TEXT_VARIATION_PASSWORD` (disable keyboard for security fields)

